        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): include requester identity in sessions_send context (Fixes #38570)",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #38570.\n\nInclude the requester agent's configured `identity.name` in the `sessions_send` agent-to-agent prompt contexts.\n\nThis updates the three A2A prompt builders used by the flow:\n\n- initial `sessions_send` request context\n- bounded ping-pong reply prompts\n- final announce prompt\n\nThe requester name is resolved from the requester session key through the configured agent identity and injected as:\n\n`Agent 1 (requester) name: <identity.name>.`\n\nThe rebased branch preserves the current prompt-cache contract from `main`: requester and target session keys still render as `<REQUESTER_SESSION>` and `<TARGET_SESSION>`, while low-cardinality channel names remain concrete.\n\nNon-goals:\n\n- no change to agent routing or access policy\n- no change to target-agent identity handling\n- no change to delivery behavior or ping-pong limits\n\n## Tests and validation\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/tools/sessions-send-helpers.test.ts`\n- `git diff --check`\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nBehavior addressed:\n\n- A2A prompt context should explicitly tell the receiving agent the requester's configured identity name instead of forcing it to infer from the session key\n\nLocal proof:\n\n- exercised the production helper surface that renders the A2A prompt text\n- added assertions for all three prompt shapes so the rendered context now includes `Agent 1 (requester) name: Stevo.`\n- kept assertions that volatile concrete session keys do not appear in the system prompt context\n\nObserved result:\n\n- helper tests passed after plumbing `requesterName` through the `sessions_send` tool and A2A flow while preserving `<REQUESTER_SESSION>` and `<TARGET_SESSION>` placeholders\n\nWhat was not tested:\n\n- a full live multi-agent exchange in a running OpenClaw session\n\nWhy this is still meaningful:\n\n- the user-visible behavior change is entirely in the prompt text built by the `sessions_send` helper flow\n- the changed tests exercise the same prompt builders used by the tool at runtime\n\n## Risk\n\nLow risk.\n\nThis only adds one extra prompt line when the requester agent has a configured `identity.name`. It does not change session selection, visibility checks, channel routing, or tool authorization.\n",
